course: dictionary
lesson: 2820
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. «Dit» is a good example. Before you choose a meaning, ask which one fits the words around it.
explain: In Morse code, «dit» is the short signal, like a dot, and «dah» is the long one. S is «dit dit dit», so you can hear SOS as «dit dit dit, dah dah dah, dit dit dit».
explain: In French, «dit» means «said» or «says». In «Jacques a dit» (Simon says), dit means said, so the game is about what Jacques said.
explain: Sailors in the UK navy have a slang meaning too: a dit is a story or yarn. When you read «dit», look at the subject and the topic first, and then test your meaning in the sentence.
fact: In Morse code, «dit» is a short signal, like a dot.
fact: In Morse code, «dah» is a long signal, like a dash.
fact: In French, «dit» means «said» or «says»: «il dit» means «he says».
fact: «C'est dit» means «that's settled».
fact: In UK navy slang, a dit is a story or yarn, as in «spin a dit».
exercise: In French, «Le chat dit miaou» means the cat ___ miaou. What does dit mean here? | Dot | Story | *Says | Dash
exercise: In Morse code, what do you call the short signal? | Dash | Long | *Dit | Dah
exercise: In UK navy slang, «spin a dit» means? | To dance | To say goodbye | *To tell a story or yarn | To send a Morse signal
test: In Morse code, SOS is «dit dit dit, dah dah dah, dit dit dit». How many dits are there in SOS? | Nine | Two | Three | *Six
test: What does «Jacques a dit» mean in English? | Jacques said goodbye | Jacques is hungry | *Simon says | Jacques is running
exam: In «Il dit, c'est dit», what does the first dit mean? | A yarn | *Says | A dot | That's settled
